mited in the current search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Overview\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they must have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Process\n\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results don't contain a dedicated CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines page or the specific review form details. The most recent specific reviewer guidelines found were for CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024. For the most current CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you may want to check the OpenReview page for CoRL 2026 or contact the CoRL 2026 organizers directly through the main CoRL website."],"durationSeconds":5.37239705}}
