{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwCkat1ZvX5eH9KXq3sM2T","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer guidelines review form criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2021 - Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://2021.corl.org/reviewer-information/instructions-for-reviewers\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2024 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's the key information:\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nACs identify desk rejection candidates, and the PC examines and makes the final decision. CoRL errs on the side of caution and only desk rejects papers when there is consensus between all PCs and the AC.\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope.\n\n### Specific Desk Rejection Reasons:\n\n1. **Formatting Issues**: Paper is either too long or in an incorrect format.\n\n2. **Anonymity Violation**: The main manuscript, supplemental materials, or a link provided in a paper identifies one or more of the authors.\n\n3. **Scope**: All CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicit intent to address a learning question for physical robots OR test the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results show the desk rejection guidelines from the official CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page, though the complete reviewer guidelines and detailed review form criteria were not fully displayed in these results. For more comprehensive information about the review form criteria and complete reviewer guidelines, you may want to visit the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb1204a1-c392-4e41-ba2c-f9f3353a30d7","uuid":"8116b9d5-564a-49e9-89b1-bebb3e0e9f3f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:25:55.226Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer guidelines review form criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KkTsSCbbgn7M2Ms4eZZuPt","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions"},{"title":"CoRL 2021 - Instructions for 