{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMToiQAH5pmE7kkUqx7G76","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale criteria dimensions site:corl2023.org\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/papers\"},{\"title\":\"Detailed Program — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/detailed-program\"},{\"title\":\"Explore Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/explore-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Workshops — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/workshops\"},{\"title\":\"Awards — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/awards\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Presenters — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/instructions-for-presenters\"},{\"title\":\"Executive Board — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/about-corl-1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here are the rating scale criteria dimensions:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\nThe specific dimensions are:\n\n1. **Originality**: Evaluates whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how it differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n2. **Quality**: Assesses whether the submission is technically sound, if claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, whether methods are appropriate, if it's a complete piece of work or work in progress, and whether authors honestly evaluate both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n3. **Clarity**: Examines whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n4. **Limitations**: CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors.\n\nThe guidelines also include **Significance** and **Relevance** as evaluation dimensions, though the detailed criteria for these specific dimensions are not fully elaborated in the retrieved content.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb1204a1-c392-4e41-ba2c-f9f3353a30d7","uuid":"db1d1a45-bd90-4c2b-a6f4-b50850d1f131","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:26:07.424Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale criteria dimensions site:corl2023.org","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TdHjVdH3qpVNiW1aeUhxqE","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/"},{"title":"Papers — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/papers"},{"title":"Detailed Program — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/detailed-program"},{"title":"Explore Papers — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/explore-papers"},{"title":"Call for Papers — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Workshops — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/workshops"},{"title":"Awards — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/awards"},{"title":"Instructions for Presenters — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/instructions-for-presenters"},{"title":"Executive Board — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/about-corl-1"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here are the rating scale criteria dimensions:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\nThe specific dimensions are:\n\n1. **Originality**: Evaluates whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how it differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n2. **Quality**: Assesses whether the submission is technically sound, if claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, whether methods are appropriate, if it's a complete piece of work or work in progress, and whether authors honestly evaluate both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n3. **Clarity**: Examines whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n4. **Limitations**: CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors.\n\nThe guidelines also include **Significance** and **Relevance** as evaluation dimensions, though the detailed criteria for these specific dimensions are not fully elaborated in the retrieved content."],"durationSeconds":6.358960427000006}}
