ined tokens: 38% target object, 16% gripper.\n\n**Table 13 (Annealing Ablation):** Annealing 0.9→0.5 vs fixed 0.5: no significant benefit (G3=0.89 vs 0.87).\n\n**Table 14 (ACIS Overhead):** +0.9% params, +1.4% FLOPs, -36.5% latency, -42% memory.\n\n**Limitations stated**: Spectral-norm Lipschitz loosens at large ε (>0.05). Physics perturbations weakest point. Temporal token selection is future work.\n\n**References**: Only 2 cited ([1] Less Is More arXiv:2601.12042, [2] CAGE ICML 2026).\n\n### Experiment Design Reference (what was planned)\n12 experiments were planned:\n1. Success Rate Evaluation (aloha_sim_insertion) — ✓ covered in Table 1\n2. LIBERO Benchmark (SmolVLA) — ✓ Table 2\n3. OpenVLA Cross-Model (LIBERO) — ✓ Table 3-4\n4. Training Ablation (Joint/Grad-Isolated/Two-Stage) — ✓ Table 6\n5. Formal Bound Verification — ✓ Table 5\n6. Cross-Compression Validation (FastV/VLA-IAP/VLA-Cache) — ✓ Table 9\n7. Defense Comparison (IMM vs AT/Smoothing/Jacobian) — ✓ Table 7\n8. Pruning Ratio Sweep — ✓ Table 10\n9. Token Importance Mechanistic Analysis — ✓ Tables 11-12\n10. Mask Ratio Annealing Ablation — ✓ Table 13\n11. ACIS Overhead Quantification — ✓ Table 14\n12. LIBERO-Plus Full Robustness — ✓ Table 8\n\nAll 12 planned experiments appear to be covered.\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a thorough review focusing on:\n1. **Method soundness**: Is the theoretical bound correct and meaningful? Are the assumptions reasonable? Is the two-stage protocol well-motivated?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Are experiments sufficient? Statistical significance? Baselines appropriate? Any missing experiments?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are implementation details sufficient?\n4. **Weaknesses**: What are the main technical concerns?\n\n## Output Format\n```\n### R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n**Summary** (3-4 sentences)\n\n**Strengths**\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Weaknesses**\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Questions for Authors**\n- Q1: ...\n- ...\n\n**Missing Experiments or Analysis**\n- ...\n\n**Minor Issues**\n- ...\n\n**Scores**\n- Originality: X/10\n- Quality: X/10\n- Clarity: X/10\n- Significance: X/10\n- Relevance: X/10\n- Overall: X/10\n- Confidence: X/5\n\n**Overall Assessment** (2-3 sentences)\n```\n","uuid":"f31e5737-e4d4-4015-9718-93318af17ac5","session_id":"bb1204a1-c392-4e41-ba2c-f9f3353a30d7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus: **Methods and Experiments**. Perform a thorough, independent review. Do NOT consult any external resources — all information you need is below.\n\n## CoRL Review Criteria\n- Rating scale 1-10 (10=top 5% seminal, 9=strong accept top 15%, 8=clear accept top 50%, 7=accept, 6=marginally above threshold, 5=marginally below, 4=reject, 3=clear reject, 2=strong reject, 1=trivial/wrong)\n- Dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n- CoRL acceptance rate: ~30-35%. CoRL requires relevance to robot learning.\n\n## Paper: \"Importance Margin Maximization: Certified Robust and Lossless Token Compression for Vision-Language-Action Models\"\n\n### Abstract\nVLA models need aggressive token compression for real-time deployment, but compressed representations are brittle under adversarial perturbations. Root cause: importance margin collapse — the gap Δ_k between retained/pruned token scores is too small. Propose IMM training framework that maximizes Δ_k, yielding first certified robustness guarantee for VLA token compression: P(top-k changes) ≤ k·ε·L/Δ_k. Two-stage training (freeze backbone→train ACIS; freeze ACIS→LoRA backbone) eliminates co-adaptation and enables lossless 50% compression that improves performance. On LIBERO, SmolVLA achieves 76.0% clean SR (+4.7pp over baseline) and 62% under combined 7-dim perturbation vs 35% undefended. Cross-model on OpenVLA (7B) confirms generality. Compression-agnostic: +51pp preservation improvement on FastV/VLA-IAP/VLA-Cache. ACIS adds 0.9% params, reduces latency 36.5%, memory 42%.\n\n### Method (Section 3)\n- **Problem Setup**: f_θ : R^{N×d} → R^N maps N visual tokens to importance scores. Compression retains top-k. Importance margin: Δ_k = s_(k) - s_(k+1).\n- **Certified Bound (Theorem 3.2)**: For L-Lipschitz f_θ and perturbation ‖δ‖ ≤ ε: P(top-k changes) ≤ k·ε·L/Δ_k. Three levers: increase Δ_k, decrease L, reduce k.\n- **IMM Loss**: L_IMM = L_action + λ·L_margin, where L_margin = max(0, γ - Δ_k) is hinge loss. γ set adaptively as percentile of current margin distribution.\n- **Two-Stage Protocol**: Stage 1: Freeze backbone, train ACIS with L_margin. Stage 2: Freeze ACIS, LoRA-finetune backbone on pruned sequences. Decouples ACIS from backbone.\n- **ACIS Architecture**: Single cross-attention head + 2-layer MLP. 2.3M params (0.9% of 256M backbone), 0.9ms latency.\n\n### Experiments (Section 4)\n**Setup**: SmolVLA (256M) primary; OpenVLA (7B) cross-model. Benchmarks: aloha_sim_insertion (60 eps), LIBERO 3 suites × 10 tasks × 20 eps, LIBERO-Plus 7-dim perturbation. Metrics: SR, action loss, G3 deploy ratio, G1 margin ratio, preservation rate.\n\n**Table 1 (aloha_sim_insertion):**\n| Method | Action Loss | SR% | 95% CI |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Baseline (no compress) | 0.00406 | 82 | 71-90 |\n| IMM prune 50% | 0.00354 | 88 | 78-94 |\n| IMM bypass (no prune) | 0.01865 | 56 | 43-68 |\n| Random prune 50% | 0.01797 | 60 | 47-72 |\n\n**Table 2 (LIBERO SmolVLA):**\n| Suite | Baseline SR% | IMM SR% | Δpp | G3 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| LIBERO-Object | 78 | 83 | +5 | 0.88 |\n| LIBERO-Spatial | 71 | 76 | +5 | 0.90 |\n| LIBERO-Goal | 65 | 69 | +4 | 0.92 |\n| LIBERO-Avg | 71.3 | 76.0 | +4.7 | 0.90 |\n\n**Table 3 (OpenVLA 7B on LIBERO):**\n| Suite | Baseline SR% | IMM SR% | Δpp | G3 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| LIBERO-Object | 82 | 86 | +4 | 0.89 |\n| LIBERO-Spatial | 76 | 80 | +4 | 0.91 |\n| LIBERO-Goal | 70 | 73 | +3 | 0.95 |\n| LIBERO-Avg | 76.0 | 79.7 | +3.7 | 0.92 |\n\n**Table 4 (Cross-Model Summary):**\n| Metric | SmolVLA | OpenVLA | Ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G1 Margin | 93.2× | 62.4× | 67% |\n| G3 Deploy | 0.90 | 0.92 | — |\n| ε-001 Preservation | 0.92 | 0.91 | 99% |\n| ACIS vs Random | 5.1× | 4.2× | 82% |\n\n**Table 5 (Formal Bound Tightness):**\n| ε | Theoretical | Empirical | Tightness | Holds? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.005 | 0.57% | 0.38% | 1.51× | ✓ |\n| 0.01 | 1.15% | 0.65% | 1.77× | ✓ |\n| 0.02 | 2.87% | 1.80% | 1.59× | ✓ |\n| 0.05 | 5.74% | 7.20% | 1.25× | ✓ |\n| 0.10 | 11.5% | 16.5% | 1.44× | ✓ |\n\n**Table 6 (Training Ablation):**\n| Strategy | Action Loss | G3 | G1 Margin | Damage |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Joint (v7) | 0.0134 | 3.19 | 57.3× | Severe |\n| Grad-Isolated (v8) | 0.00546 | 1.34 | 50.2× | Moderate |\n| Two-Stage (v8b) | 0.00354 | 0.87 | 93.2× | None |\n| Baseline | 0.00406 | — | 1.0× | N/A |\n\n**Table 7 (Defense Comparison, LIBERO-Avg SmolVLA):**\n| Defense | Clean SR% | Pert. SR% | Drop (pp) | Cost (GPU-h) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| No defense | 71.3 | 48 | 23.3 | 0 |\n| Adversarial Training | 68 | 63 | 5 | 45 |\n| Rand. Smoothing | 70 | 61 | 9 | 0 |\n| Jacobian Reg. | 72 | 65 | 7 | 35 |\n| IMM (ours) | 76 | 71 | 5 | 30 |\n\n**Table 8 (LIBERO-Plus 7-dim):**\n| Perturbation | IMM SR% | No Def SR% | IMM Δpp | No Def Δpp |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Clean | 76 | 71.3 | — | — |\n| Lighting | 73 | 58 | -3 | -13 |\n| Camera Pose | 70 | 52 | -6 | -19 |\n| Texture | 74 | 60 | -2 | -11 |\n| Distractor | 72 | 55 | -4 | -16 |\n| Background | 75 | 62 | -1 | -9 |\n| Physics | 68 | 46 | -8 | -25 |\n| Combined | 62 | 35 | -14 | -36 |\n\n**Table 9 (Cross-Compression):**\n| Method | Loss (base) | Loss (+IMM) | Pres. (base) | Pres. (+IMM) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| FastV | 0.0058 | 0.0048 | 41% | 89% |\n| VLA-IAP | 0.0052 | 0.0044 | 38% | 90% |\n| VLA-Cache | 0.0063 | 0.0051 | 35% | 87% |\n| ACIS (ours) | 0.0041 | 0.0035 | 34% | 92% |\n\n**Table 10 (Pruning Ratio Sweep):**\nKeep ratios 0.3-0.9 tested. U-shaped G3 curve, sweet spot at 0.4-0.6. Optimal at 0.55 (G3=0.83, SR=90%).\n\n**Tables 11-12 (Mechanistic Analysis):**\nPruned tokens: 4× lower attention, 7.4× less gradient contribution, 3.2% action loss contribution. 83% from background regions. Retained tokens: 38% target object, 16% gripper.\n\n**Table 13 (Annealing Ablation):** Annealing 0.9→0.5 vs fixed 0.5: no significant benefit (G3=0.89 vs 0.87).\n\n**Table 14 (ACIS Overhead):** +0.9% params, +1.4% FLOPs, -36.5% latency, -42% memory.\n\n**Limitations stated**: Spectral-norm Lipschitz loosens at large ε (>0.05). Physics perturbations weakest point. Temporal token selection is future work.\n\n**References**: Only 2 cited ([1] Less Is More arXiv:2601.12042, [2] CAGE ICML 2026).\n\n### Experiment Design Reference (what was planned)\n12 experiments were planned:\n1. Success Rate Evaluation (aloha_sim_insertion) — ✓ covered in Table 1\n2. LIBERO Benchmark (SmolVLA) — ✓ Table 2\n3. OpenVLA Cross-Model (LIBERO) — ✓ Table 3-4\n4. Training Ablation (Joint/Grad-Isolated/Two-Stage) — ✓ Table 6\n5. Formal Bound Verification — ✓ Table 5\n6. Cross-Compression Validation (FastV/VLA-IAP/VLA-Cache) — ✓ Table 9\n7. Defense Comparison (IMM vs AT/Smoothing/Jacobian) — ✓ Table 7\n8. Pruning Ratio Sweep — ✓ Table 10\n9. Token Importance Mechanistic Analysis — ✓ Tables 11-12\n10. Mask Ratio Annealing Ablation — ✓ Table 13\n11. ACIS Overhead Quantification — ✓ Table 14\n12. LIBERO-Plus Full Robustness — ✓ Table 8\n\nAll 12 planned experiments appear to be covered.\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a thorough review focusing on:\n1. **Method soundness**: Is the theoretical bound correct and meaningful? Are the assumptions reasonable? Is the two-stage protocol well-motivated?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Are experiments sufficient? Statistical significance? Baselines appropriate? Any missing experiments?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are implementation details sufficient?\n4. **Weaknesses**: What are the main technical concerns?\n\n## Output Format\n```\n### R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n**Summary** (3-4 sentences)\n\n**Strengths**\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Weaknesses**\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Questions for Authors**\n- Q1: ...\n- ...\n\n**Missing Experiments or Analysis**\n- ...\n\n**Minor Issues**\n- ...\n\n**Scores**\n- Originality: X/10\n- Quality: X/10\n- Clarity: X/10\n- Significance: X/10\n- Relevance: X/10\n- Overall: X/10\n- Confidence: X/5\n\n**Overall Assessment** (2-3 sentences)\n```\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QjDroLaKHUxdDKfWJLx5PN","session_id":"bb1204a1-c392-4e41-ba2c-f9f3353a30d7","uuid":"5f3f1591-2b52-4a27-b7c2-9da679f5a47e","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:27:32.247Z"}
